From 0e25954da984d9c2b2383f4ab046b8ed72bf731a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flip-engineer <will.a.hargis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:54:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Admit native builds through one shared lock and capacity
 receipt

build-native.sh now re-execs through build-admission.py. Full coordinator
generation takes an exclusive flock under the Git common directory; focused
builds take a shared lock. Admission refuses immediately with exact observed
capacity when another generation holds the lock or actual memory and disk are
below the recorded minimum. Each attempt retains a JSON receipt with source,
toolchain, cgroup, capacity, pid and pgid, and exit or forwarded signal. The
child runs in its own session, so cancellation reaches the whole process tree.

Issue #677 records the duplicate Main generation recurrence; #819 requires
host-capacity admission. The wrapper does not impose a cgroup memory bound
because it cannot create one without runner privilege; the receipt records the
inherited cgroup and memory.max for the workflow admission.

Tests use tiny sleep and exit fixtures only, under the 8 GiB test cap.
---
 bend2/scripts/build-admission.py | 260 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 bend2/scripts/build-native.sh    |   6 +
 bend2/test/build-admission.py    | 135 ++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 401 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 bend2/scripts/build-admission.py
